  "conventions": [
    "Deterministic objectives; optional observation noise is not added.",
    "Recommended domains are metadata, not clipping constraints.",
    "Hartmann-6 names follow the displayed equations: standard -sum; rescaled (-sum-2.58)/1.94. SFU MATLAB code links appear reversed.",
    "Sphere6-rescaled follows the displayed weighted equation (sum(2^i*x_i^2)-1745)/899 on the stated unit cube. Its stated zero-mean/unit-variance description does not follow from that equation; no undocumented input transform is applied.",
    "Langermann uses the positive sum displayed by SFU, unlike the negative sum in SciPy.",
    "Hartmann3 uses SFU P[4,1]=0.0381; SciPy uses 0.03815.",
    "Shekel uses SFU center [5,3,5,3]; SciPy uses [5,5,3,3].",
    "Colville uses SFU first term 100*(x1^2-x2)^2; the pinned SciPy source instead uses 100*(x1-x2^2)^2.",
    "Schwefel uses SFU constant 418.9829; the pinned SciPy source uses 418.982887.",
    "Powell supports dimensions divisible by four, summing independent four-coordinate blocks.",
    "Reference fixture generation records adaptations in tests/generate_reference.py; tests run offline against frozen values."
  ],
